 },
 "parts": [
  "Why does an airplane window have a tiny hole?",
  "It is not a defect.",
  "The window is not one piece of plastic.",
  "It is a stack of three acrylic layers.",
  "The inner one is a scratch pane. It protects. It is not structural.",
  "The tiny hole is in the middle layer.",
  "It lets cabin pressure reach the gap next to the outer layer.",
  "So the pressure load falls on the outer layer.",
  "If the outer one ever failed, the middle layer is the backup.",
  "Engineers call that fail-safe design.",
  "The hole also lets moisture out, according to Boeing.",
  "That helps keep the window clear of fog and frost.",
  "Sometimes a ring of frost shows around it.",
  "A tiny hole with a quiet job."
 ],
